      "answer": "$6\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\mathrm{m}$ ($\\frac{20}{3}\\,\\mathrm{m}$)",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "B1: $Q$ takes 0.7 s from $B$ to $C$.\nB1FT (SOI): $0.4=\\frac{(\\text{their }2)+0}{2}t\\Rightarrow t=0.4$; FT their 2 from (b), equivalently $t=0.8/(\\text{their }2)$. Use $s=((u+v)/2)t$ for a time up the slope; allow total slope time from $0=(\\text{their }2)t-\\tfrac12(\\text{their }a)t^2\\Rightarrow t=0.8$.\nB1: The intermediate distance moved by $P$ is $(0.7+0.8)\\times4=6$ m; allow 1 m from point $C$.\nM1: Set up and solve an equation in $t$ using $4t$, $(\\text{their }2)t$ and their 6, considering all parts of motion: $4t+(\\text{their }2)t=(\\text{their }1)$ OR $(\\text{their }6)+4t+(\\text{their }2)t=7$.\nA1: Final distance from $B=6\\frac{2}{3}$ m.\nAlternative method for last three marks: B1 $[\\text{Time for }P]=b/4$ and $[\\text{Time for }QR]=(7-b)/2$, where $b$ is distance from $B$; OR $[\\text{Time for }P]=(7-c)/4$ and $[\\text{Time for }QR]=c/2$, where $c$ is distance from $C$. M1 form and solve the total-time equation, considering all parts of motion: $(7-b)/2+0.7+0.4+0.4=b/4\\Rightarrow b=6\\frac{2}{3}$, OR $c/2+0.7+0.4+0.4=(7-c)/4\\Rightarrow c=1/3$. A1 final distance from $B=6\\frac{2}{3}$ m.\nPrinted total: 5.",
